# Stage4 LIVE-ONLY package list — Orange Pi 3 LTS (Allwinner H6, arm64).
# One atom per line; lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Appended by build-orangepi3-lts-stage4.sh ONLY when a bootable flavor is
# being built (BUILD_LIVE or BUILD_INSTALLER: --flavor live | installer | both).
# The LIVE flavor boots a squashfs rootfs ephemerally; that requires a dracut
# dmsquash-live initramfs to find the live medium, mount LiveOS/squashfs.img
# read-only, and stack a writable tmpfs overlay as the ephemeral root. The bare
# kernel canNOT interpret root=live: / rd.live.* on its own — those are dracut
# directives — so dracut must be present in the cross sysroot to GENERATE that
# initramfs at build time. Mirrors specs-frite/specs-orangepi5's identical
# packages-live.list.
#
# The INSTALLER flavor's OWN medium is ALSO a live boot (see the builder's
# build_installer_iso), so dracut is needed whenever EITHER bootable flavor is
# selected; it stays out of the always-installed base set and is added here.

# dracut: builds the dmsquash-live initramfs (and, for --encrypt-root, the
# separate disk-boot crypt-capable initramfs). The builder invokes it as a host
# tool pointed at the aarch64 sysroot (qemu-chroot preferred; see the builder).
sys-kernel/dracut
